  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: COC3_Quiz_LO3_Testing_Q05
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: The test is signed in as student01 rather than as an administrator.
    Why does that matter?
  choices:
  - Administrators cannot use Remote Desktop
  - An administrator can always connect, so it would prove nothing about the permission
  - Administrator sessions are not logged
  - The administrator account has no redirected Documents folder
  correctChoiceIndex: 1
  points: 10
  explanation: Administrators bypass the very setting being tested. A test that only
    passes for an administrator has tested nothing.
